WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.548
Scan receipts into a spreadsheet without uploading them.

2
00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:11.288
How on-device OCR reads a receipt photo, how the shop, date, tax and total

3
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:16.245
are picked out, and tips for scans that come out right the first time.

4
00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:22.773
Step 1: clean up the photo. Text recognition works best on dark text on

5
00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:25.517
a light background with good contrast.

6
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:29.333
Step 2: read the text with OCR.

7
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:35.094
The reading is done by Tesseract, an open source OCR engine that uses a

8
00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:40.044
small LSTM neural network trained to recognise lines of text.

9
00:00:41.344 --> 00:00:46.488
Using the results. Each receipt shows its photo next to editable fields

10
00:00:46.488 --> 00:00:48.661
for shop, date, tax and total.

11
00:00:49.961 --> 00:00:54.853
Privacy. Receipts can show your card's last digits, your address for deliveries,

12
00:00:54.853 --> 00:00:56.809
and where you were at what time.

13
00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:01.454
To try it, open AI Receipt Scanner in OpenFile.

14
00:01:01.454 --> 00:01:05.510
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:09.139
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:15.647
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
